# kex: check-only
# The standard streams are `FileHandle` values, so their typestate is the same
# check a file opened `FS.Read` gets (kexhq/kex#139).
#
# `IO.out` and `IO.error` are `FileHandle<CannotRead, CanWrite>`, `IO.in`
# is `FileHandle<CanRead, CannotWrite>`. Writing to stdin or reading from
# stdout is rejected here, not at runtime.

main do
  IO.in.printLine("stdin is not a sink")
  IO.out.getLine
  IO.error.read
end
